Memory extraction and dream wait for an idle session

Managed auto-memory extraction and dream started right after every answer.
They are model calls of their own, so they ran in parallel with the user's
next question (on a single-stream local server both decoded at a fraction
of their speed) and their side prompt could take the conversation's place in
a provider's prompt cache. Where a next question can come (interactive and
ACP sessions) they now start only after the session has been idle for 10
seconds (QWEN_CODE_MEMORY_EXTRACT_IDLE_MS; MARIADB_CODE_MEMORY_EXTRACT_IDLE_MS
in MariaDB Code); a new question restarts the wait, and the next idle period
covers both turns (extraction resumes from its cursor). Headless runs start
them right away as before. A pending start is dropped on shutdown, like any
new background memory work. ACP sessions that end a turn outside the client's
agent loop (the default) start them through the client as well
(scheduleManagedMemoryRun), and a fresh prompt cancels the pending start.

